{
    "background_story": "Paulina was a free-spirited herbalist who spent most of her life studying the ancient properties of plants. She was particularly fascinated by the sassafras tree, with its unique mitten-shaped leaves and aromatic bark. Growing up in the rural South, Paulina learned from her grandmother how to harvest sassafras roots to make traditional teas and remedies. As she delved deeper into her research, Paulina discovered the tree's potential to heal and protect. She spent years cultivating sassafras on her own land, experimenting with its uses and sharing her knowledge with the community. Paulina's sassafras farm became a beloved gathering place, where people would come to learn about the natural world and find solace in the beauty of nature. Her dedication to the sassafras tree earned her the nickname 'Sassafras Queen,' a testament to her passion and expertise.",
